WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.408 --> 00:00:02.730
- [Man] Amsterdam, Netherlands.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:05.920
Famous for its stroopwafle
or stroopwafles,

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:07.690
its marijuana (coughing),

00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:09.700
I mean baked goods.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:13.100
And it's delicious, slippery
raw fish known as herring.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.540
More importantly, Dutch new herring.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:19.700
Yep, that's a headless raw fish. (ewing)

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:21.983
This one's gonna be delicious.

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:26.460
This is probably the most
famous dish in the Netherlands.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:30.030
But to understand why we must
travel to the dish's origin.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:31.900
Welcome to Scheveningen-

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.680
the seaside town obsessed
with the herring,

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:37.770
illustrated by this giant
herring eating statue.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:40.980
I mean their town's flag even
has three herrings on it.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.050
Oh wait, sorry, that's a
bad example; there we go.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.843
Meet Cees. He's the
owner of Haring Huisje.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:33.320
- [Man] And chomp.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.989
So let's go back to Amsterdam.

00:01:34.989 --> 00:01:35.822
(bell ringing)

00:01:35.822 --> 00:01:37.963
Here they eat the herring
a little differently.

00:01:46.031 --> 00:01:49.281
- [Man] But why the pickles and onions.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.950
- [Man] The dish can't
be found in restaurants-

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:05.000
only these last surviving herring stores

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.453
scattered around the dam.

00:02:19.046 --> 00:02:21.463
(screeching)

00:02:23.077 --> 00:02:25.244
(dinging)

00:02:32.504 --> 00:02:33.802
(relax grunting)

00:02:33.802 --> 00:02:36.052
- [Man] OK, wish me luck.

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:43.766
(light ragtime music)

00:02:48.092 --> 00:02:51.092
(light electronica)

